# EdminBoost ANM Compliance

Gate before presenting final code. If any checklist item is "no", fix it first.

See `edminboost-anm-project.mdc`, `edminboost-anm-standards.mdc`, `edminboost-anm-wordpress-php.mdc`.

## Security

- Sanitize on input, escape on output, authorize before action, verify nonce before write.
- Never trust browser or request input.
- Use `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::CAPABILITY` on site admin pages and privileged handlers; network admin screens and `context=network` AJAX use `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::NETWORK_CAPABILITY` (`manage_network_options`).
- Settings API: `sanitize_callback` via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize()`, `show_in_rest => false`. Network default settings use `sanitize_network_settings()`; network policy uses `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::sanitize_policy()`. Site `sanitize()` returns stored raw unchanged when multisite policy forbids site edits (non–network-admin save).
- AJAX: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ajax::verify_request()` — `check_ajax_referer( 'edminboost_anm_admin', 'nonce' )` + capability check (`manage_options` for site context, `manage_network_options` when posted `context` is `network`). Site settings mutations (e.g. Quick Status toggle) use `verify_site_settings_mutation()` — also blocks when `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::site_can_edit_settings()` is false. Mirror pattern for new actions.
- Inbox sort/filter AJAX (`edminboost_anm_inbox_list`): same verification; returned row HTML must escape all notice fields in the partial.
- Debug seed/trigger AJAX: `verify_debug_request()` — requires `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Debug::is_available()`.
- Rule export: `admin_post_edminboost_anm_export_rules` — nonce + capability before download.
- SQL: `$wpdb->prepare()` only; prefer Options API (`edminboost_anm_*`) over custom tables.
- Inbox notice HTML: treat as untrusted; use `wp_kses_post()` or equivalent on display; sanitize fields on capture.
- Notice hide AJAX (`edminboost_anm_notice_hide`, `edminboost_anm_reset_hidden_notices`): same `verify_request()` + capability; sanitize scope/hash inputs; persist preferences in options/user meta only.
- Digest preview AJAX (`edminboost_anm_digest_preview`): `verify_request()`; sanitize posted `digest` via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize_digest_settings()` merged with stored digest (including `send_weekday`, recipients via `sanitize_digest_recipients()`); return preview only — no `wp_mail()` on preview.
- Inbox snooze/read AJAX (`edminboost_anm_inbox_action`): same `verify_request()`; sanitize notice id and duration keys; snooze toggle must not bypass capability checks.
- Webhook preview AJAX (`edminboost_anm_webhook_preview`): `verify_request()`; sanitize posted webhook fields via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize_webhook_settings()` merged with stored webhook (preview UI typically posts unsaved `message` only); return preview only — no `wp_remote_post()` on preview.
- Digest/webhook settings: `sanitize_digest_settings()` and `sanitize_webhook_settings()` on Settings API save (both merge with stored values; only posted keys override). Digest preview AJAX uses `sanitize_digest_settings()` against current stored digest; webhook preview AJAX uses `sanitize_webhook_settings()` with partial input (typically unsaved `message` only — URL/enabled preserved when omitted). Webhook URLs: `sanitize_webhook_url()` (http/https + `wp_http_validate_url()`) on save and before `wp_remote_post()`.
- Block ad redirects: sanitize URL list in `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize_block_ad_redirect_urls()`; admin-only `wp_safe_redirect` — no outbound requests.

## Directory & Privacy

- No obfuscated code, undisclosed telemetry, or hidden external requests.
- No tracking or analytics to vendor servers. Docs link is user-initiated only.
- **Webhook** (`settings.webhook`): disabled by default; user supplies URL; sends notice summary JSON via `wp_remote_post` only when enabled. Document in `readme.txt`.
- **Digest**: uses `wp_mail()` to configured recipients — no third-party email API.
- No spammy readme or deceptive behavior.
- Any new remote integration must be documented, justified, and opt-in.

## Code Quality

- Prefer WordPress core APIs over custom hacks.
- Keep code human-readable for directory review.
- Follow WPCS across PHP, CSS, JS, and HTML.
- Admin-only unless explicitly requested; enqueue plugin-screen assets via `is_plugin_screen()` (and `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::is_network_plugin_screen()` on multisite).
- Interceptor script loads on wp-admin when plugin is enabled — keep payload minimal; no external script URLs.
- Use `edminboost_anm` / `EDMINBOOST_ANM_` prefix consistently.

## Self-Review Checklist

- [ ] No WordPress core modifications
- [ ] GPL-compatible
- [ ] Human-readable, reviewable code
- [ ] User-facing strings translatable (`EDMINBOOST_ANM_TEXT_DOMAIN`)
- [ ] Privileged actions: capability checks (+ nonces for AJAX/admin-post)
- [ ] Input sanitized; output escaped
- [ ] SQL prepared (if any)
- [ ] Assets scoped; admin notices minimal and dismissible
- [ ] Webhook/digest behavior documented; webhook off by default
- [ ] Uninstall path removes plugin data (per-site options; multisite sitemeta via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Multisite::uninstall_all_sites()`) and clears digest cron
- [ ] Unique `EDMINBOOST_ANM_` / `edminboost_anm_` prefix; maintainable structure
- [ ] Would survive WordPress.org review

## Unsafe Requests

If a feature conflicts with the Plugin Handbook, Coding Standards, security best practices, privacy expectations, or Directory Guidelines — refuse the unsafe approach and propose a compliant alternative.
